(1) on Dev, api and worker connect as cis_app, and a forged foreign app.tenant_id on the main pool returns 0 rows from every RLS table;
(2) migrations, schema dump, TripPlanner/catalog reads, photo sync and the job runner all work;
(3) the rollback path is documented and tested once.
AA-852 (In Progress) is the parent chain for waves 1–3, and all of those are shipped. The execution plan is root docs/audits/2026-10-17-S241-x1/x1-plan.md: rev 2, the "S242 amendments" block wins over the step text. S15 is CIS code prep. S16 is CIS 244 (cis_app grants, default privileges, D2 policies). S17 is Nghiệp's Console DSN plus DB Migrate set-password. S18 switches api and worker DATABASE_URL to aa-cis/dev/rds-cis-app. S19 adds a Deny on the master and other-app secrets for the CIS task role. S20 is rl-002 (cis_owner, db_migrator). S21 is CIS 245 (ownership to cis_owner). S22 makes db_migrator the DB Migrate login, adds the 246 probe and ends the catalog.* view freeze (XD9). S23 is close-out.
Backlog row #2 (docs/backlog/README.md:36) says probe 39 pass / 16 pending / 0 fail, and the catalog.* view freeze holds until S22 (backlog line 13).
CRITICAL FINDING, the plan is wrong on one point. x1-plan §1.4 and S16 item 3 say FORCE RLS already filters the master, so a non-owner cis_app needs no policy on the 8 FORCE tables. The 244 guard in the plan even asserts published_tours without a GUC = 0. The live AA-817 probe disagrees. docs/audits/2026-10-16-S239-in-progress-audit/aa817-done-evidence/probe_v2_after_239.json shows, for aa_cis_admin, rls_active=false and foreign_guc == total on all 8 FORCE tables: published_tours 892/892, raw_tours 987/987, generated_content 1481/1481, quality_scores 1481/1481, seo_context 918/918, pipeline_runs 46/46. Critique point 4 and lesson S236 agree, and so does the AA-860 description. Only about 6 CIS files set app.tenant_id, while about 69 files read FORCE tables. If S16/S18 follow the plan, cis_app reads 0 rows and its writes are refused on raw_tours, published_tours, generated_content and the rest, which breaks the whole pipeline and admin. S16 must therefore add parity policies TO cis_app on the 8 FORCE tables as well, and S21 (245) must handle cis_owner the same way. Because of this, Done-when (1) cannot be met as worded while admin needs cross-tenant reads on the main pool. Nghiệp has to amend it (see blockers).

